      "summary": "Hi there! 👋 I'm Sooraj Vijayan T K.\n\nI’m a Software Engineer with 4+ years of experience specializing in frontend development using React.js, with hands-on backend exposure (Node.js & Express.js) in building scalable, real-world applications.\n\nMy core strength lies in building performant, user-focused web applications using modern JavaScript frameworks. I have extensive experience working with React.js, Next.js, TypeScript, and modern UI libraries to deliver responsive, maintainable, and scalable interfaces. I’m comfortable working closely with APIs, state management solutions, and backend services to deliver end-to-end features.\n\nPreviously, at Revyrie Global, I work on multiple high-impact products:\n\n- Blob AI, an AI-powered chat platform integrating OpenAI GPT-4o, real-time responses using Server-Sent Events (SSE), role-based access control, and Stripe subscription workflows.\n- Everle Admin Panel, where I built the admin system from scratch, implemented real-time bug notification systems, and developed analytics dashboards for business metrics like CAC, LTV, and active subscribers.\n- Lyfe, a secure document management platform with AI-driven summarization, real-time updates using Firebase, and client-side API encryption for enhanced security.\n\nPreviously at Hamon Technologies, I worked on:\n- EV charging and insurance platforms, developing responsive admin dashboards, reusable table components with sorting and filtering, and Redux-based state management.\n- Giblib, a US-based medical education platform, where I contributed to full-stack features, video upload workflows, and real-time user messaging systems.\n\nWhat I bring:\n- Strong expertise in React.js ecosystem (Hooks, performance optimization, reusable components)\n- Solid understanding of state management (Redux, Zustand)\n- Backend experience with Node.js, Express.js, REST APIs\n- Experience integrating authentication, payments, real-time systems, and AI services\n- A product-focused mindset with attention to performance, security, and user experience\n\nI enjoy working on challenging frontend problems, collaborating with cross-functional teams, and building products that scale. I’m currently open to frontend-focused or full-stack-leaning roles where I can contribute to impactful products and continue growing technically.",
